ne a broadside and a  mortar that allows you to basically you  know do an additional damage from long  range going back a little bit to when  you said you as you're becoming a pirate  and you're becoming more and more  infamous how is that going to be  reflected in the game is it going to be  like cosmetic or is it gonna be you know  like a realm of influence that perhaps  other players can see yes so yes all  those things the biggest thing is that  when you do something in the world the  world has it has an impact it reacts I  want personally and I hope that other  people feel the same way as pirates I  want people to see my ship see my  accomplishments be afraid of me  because they can see that I've done or  accomplished things that they haven't  dreamed of I want them to be jealous of  my figurehead jealous of my sails see my  guild pattern and my pirate you know  gang flag and be scared of me and those  are things that are done through  customization and progression you talk  about this open world that the open sea  how big are we are we talking how much  of it is is explorable where can I sail  well the mode that you see in the demo  is Madagascar that's the first area that  we're exposing but you know stay tuned  in the coming months we'll talk about it  more but look at a map of the Indian  Ocean and dream because that's what  we're doing we look at it we think how  can we bring people to really end  locations that are exotic that they've  never been to in any game ever that  really reflect the age of piracy and and  all of the things that took place in  this world it's full of ton of stories  and we want to help players not only  experience stories like that but form  their own that they can tell other  people that that will you know propel  them on their own journeys you talk  about visiting taverns and stuff that  was that gonna be something that you  explore on foot as your captain or is it  going to be like a UI menu thing how is  that going to work we'll talk more in a  couple months but what we want players  to understand specifically is we have a  hideout your hideout is the basically  the linchpin of the pirate fantasy it's  where you handle your upgrades you  collect new ships you personalize and  customize those ships you meet new  characters and as well as meeting people  in the tavern and getting information  and Intel about the world before you  plan your heist there's other  opportunities for us to create that sort  of experience within the world but this  is kind of where we're at right now  we're showing people the loot hunt mode  so they can really dream about the  fantasy of being a pirate at the helm of  their ship in terms of so like if Dave  and I were going to play we'll be able  to play together on one ship or is it I  have a ship and he has ship every  captain has their own ship all right  every captain is able to customize it to  their a preference the cool thing about  it is if you guys were playing together  you could plan your synergies like okay  this ship works well with this make sure  you bring this this can in I'll bring a  mortar that will slow and stun my you  know enemy and and now let's work  together this hunt and exploit the trade  routes together those synergies we think  really add the complexity and depth and  if you look at the demo you can see that  there's a really really heavy influence  of the wind in our world and that wind  that topology on our level design allows  players to take advantage of it through  positioning and understanding the speed  of their enemy and being able to  overtake your enemy by meeting smarter  with him and using the wind it's it's a  really cool thing we're seeing even now  while people are playing it live at e3  now being a captain of a ship obviously  being at the helm of a vessel is  obviously just one of the roles that you  take you've got a Cutlass at your side  you've got a blunderbuss are we going to  see anything when it comes to like  swordplay gunplay combat or is it all  going to be shipped to ship based well  we're focused again we're focused really  on making sure people understand the  naval combat that we're trying to expose  the depth we're not black flag  in gameplay we have much deeper  complexity in terms of our combat we  have boarding boarding for us as a  high-risk high-reward maneuver you're  seeing a little taste of it in  multiplayer now and you know as we start  to release more and more about the game  you're going to find out more about  everything you can do as a pirate how  you can take over your enemies and how  you can basically put them at the tip of  your sword and at the end of your cannon  mmm one of the things I noticed in the  trailer that I'm very glad is returning  other shanties absolutely uh every  shanty that you hear in the game will be  a brand new recording we have really an  amazing tone amazing feeling the  ambience you have I think three shanties  that you can hear in all of our assets  now of the new ones as well as ones that  will unfold specifically about the  Indian Ocean and such so we're really  excited everybody loves shanties and we  want it we were really proud to be able  to bring it back to two scholar modes  when you come sorry go ahead with a  shanties that you've researched and like  actually with song of the time or if you  kind of modified and added a couple of  your own well the shanties were  primarily work songs they were designed  to you know allow the crew to have a  proper cadence let them know what type  of work need to be done and to really  invigorate the crew while they were  doing their work and that's what they  are in our game we're also exploring  ways to bring new music and tones from  the world people should feel as if  they're not listening into a soundtrack  that's outside the world but that the  world is speaking to them and shanties  are a critical part of that unification  between the captain the quartermaster  and the crew so when it comes to a  multiplayer are you going to be doing  something similar to foreigner where you  gain control of areas there's the  seasons involved in the world kind of  adapts to who's winning yes seasons are  a key part in skull and bones of our  progression to become the ultimate  pirate king kingpin you compete against  other pirates and part of that is being  able to have the right gang defeat your  enemies and really master the trade  routes against your competitors so as  you grow and you customize your ship  even further  are they purely cosmetic upgrades are  they like so if they're for example is  someone who's super good at the game you  know get all the top tier upgrades what  can newer players maybe do to combat  that or they  to the matchmaking maybe not put in the  same well I mean we will have  matchmaking so that you have the best  time possible but our PvP is horizontal  and the progression is based on choice  and and your skill  I don't want players to play and I don't  think anybody wants to play a game where  they're outgunned but just because  someone played longer than them and we  want it to be something where over time  you develop the right ship the right  configuration the right customization  for how you want to play in your play  style but it's not a vertical race in  our you know our shared systemic world  of course we're going to push you  through a progression that allows you to  meet new challenges and always have  something in front of you that's tougher  and tougher and against other players  we're going to make sure it's fair now  when obviously pirates say they had a  lot of loot on board if they've been  doing their job right and you mentioned  having a hideout is there going to be  like a risk system if your ships become  full you need to get your hideout to  stowaway loot up or hide it somewhere is  it possible for your ship to be sunk and  lose all your hard-earned gold  okay so piracy is risk versus reward and  in o