ell you got dozens of languages spoke  in the studio and you have a huge  connection between all of these  developers from different backgrounds  working within the same vision of  bringing this game to life and it's so  exciting like I saw pictures and videos  of our reveal after the fact and it's  just amazing to see everybody react the  way that they did so we're all super  proud one thing that was a little  surprising you talked a lot about the  research and it's very grounded in  reality but then in the end we see a  rather large squid a Kraken yeah I'm at  the time you know first of all sailors  believed in all sorts of stuff and one  of the things that they feared most was  things like the Kraken and our world  reflects the sensibility of the sailors  of the day and the pirates of the day if  you look at maps from the 14th through  17th century there's things in the  corner of the map that the sailors  saying don't go there that there's  danger you know and that's that feeling  we want we want players to be totally  afraid of that type of creature  appearing out of nowhere and pulling  them under you're already playing  towards not both the history and the  reality of pirates but also their  superstitions absolutely the world is  seen through the eyes of the pirates of  the day and that's how we want you to  feel we want you to you know to take a  little journey with us to the Golden Age  of piracy in the Indian Ocean and really  feel like you're in a world that  responds and reacts to everything that  happens and it's a real place so you  said the people getting the hands on it  on the show floor they're going to be  beaches that people can sign up for yeah  absolutely we have live phases that are  coming soon you can register for that at  Skull and Bones game.com and for us we  are a pirate crew and our community is  going to be built on people who want to  have the ultimate pirate game we don't  want to leave anybody behind your voice  is important so if y